WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.714
A password is a secret you hand
over. To every site, every time.

00:00:07.114 --> 00:00:11.228
Sites keep copies. Fake
sites ask just as nicely.

00:00:11.628 --> 00:00:16.193
A passkey isn't a secret you share. It's
a signature only your device can make.

00:00:16.593 --> 00:00:20.253
Your device makes a pair of
keys. The private key never

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:24.312
leaves it, and only your face,
fingerprint or PIN unlocks it.

00:00:24.712 --> 00:00:27.669
The site keeps only the public key. It can

00:00:27.669 --> 00:00:30.627
check your signature, but never forge one.

00:00:31.027 --> 00:00:33.397
To sign in, the site sends a fresh

00:00:33.397 --> 00:00:37.091
challenge. Your device signs
it, and the site checks.

00:00:37.491 --> 00:00:43.079
No secret crosses the wire. A
stolen public key signs no one in.

00:00:43.479 --> 00:00:48.616
Each passkey is bound to the real site's
domain. A lookalike gets nothing.

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:53.358
Your keychain or password manager
syncs them across your devices.

00:00:53.758 --> 00:00:59.909
Stop handing over secrets. Look for
"Create a passkey" in your settings.

